WEBVTT

00:00:32.010 --> 00:00:35.510
<i>I must do it.</i>

00:00:47.010 --> 00:00:50.190
The future everyone dreamed of,

00:00:50.610 --> 00:00:55.470
an ideal, peaceful age where science solves everything.

00:00:57.870 --> 00:01:05.240
Most of the energy for cars, bikes, and factories comes from the sky,

00:01:05.240 --> 00:01:09.460
so we don't have to fight over resources.

00:01:09.460 --> 00:01:14.570
It's all thanks to the Manifestor Engine that was completed 5 years ago.

00:01:17.100 --> 00:01:23.260
The Manifestor Engine is on an artificial island in Sagami Bay, Blue Island.

00:01:23.260 --> 00:01:28.480
It provides energy all around the world through a network of satellites.

00:01:39.330 --> 00:01:42.410
I'm glad to see you're doing fine, Akane.

00:01:42.410 --> 00:01:45.160
Good morning, Mrs. Suzuki!

00:01:45.840 --> 00:01:48.520
We sure can see the Engine clearly this morning.

00:01:48.520 --> 00:01:50.360
The weather should be lovely today.

00:01:50.360 --> 00:01:50.920
Yeah!

00:01:51.880 --> 00:01:55.340
Actually, the inventor of the Engine is none other than my granddad.

00:02:02.800 --> 00:02:04.810
He built me this thing too.

00:02:05.680 --> 00:02:08.270
The one and only flying bike in the world.

00:02:08.270 --> 00:02:10.560
I call it Doggy.

00:02:13.460 --> 00:02:17.080
The elderly say we're living in a great age.

00:02:17.470 --> 00:02:20.110
And I'm sure they're right!

00:02:22.150 --> 00:02:24.580
So I love everything here!

00:02:25.350 --> 00:02:27.940
This island, and all the people!

00:02:30.460 --> 00:02:33.490
<i>I will be arriving at Blue Island this afternoon.</i>

00:02:33.490 --> 00:02:35.760
<i>I am looking forward to meeting you!</i>

00:02:36.200 --> 00:02:38.810
<i>See you soon! Aoi.</i>

00:02:43.320 --> 00:02:44.890
Oh, hello?

00:02:44.890 --> 00:02:47.400
Sis, breakfast's ready.

00:02:47.400 --> 00:02:48.860
Okies!

00:03:39.680 --> 00:03:42.310
Sis, bring out the miso soup, please!

00:03:42.310 --> 00:03:43.460
Sure!

00:03:43.960 --> 00:03:46.770
Whoa, you put okra in it!

00:03:46.770 --> 00:03:49.020
Fresh from the garden this morning.

00:03:49.020 --> 00:03:50.130
Yay!

00:03:50.770 --> 00:03:52.760
Okra, okra, ok—

00:03:56.430 --> 00:03:58.260
Good morning, Dad.

00:03:59.690 --> 00:04:02.940
Sis, call Gramps please!

00:04:02.940 --> 00:04:03.520
Going!

00:04:08.000 --> 00:04:09.480
Gramps!

00:04:09.980 --> 00:04:13.990
Dr. Isshiki Kenjiro! Breakfast is ready!

00:04:21.440 --> 00:04:26.590
Who dares disturb my research?!

00:04:26.590 --> 00:04:28.960
Your granddaughter!

00:04:30.540 --> 00:04:32.720
Indeed, you're my granddaughter, Akane!

00:04:33.720 --> 00:04:36.500
It's been 8 hours, 57 minutes and 12 seconds!

00:04:37.090 --> 00:04:38.760
I'm so happy to see you!

00:04:38.760 --> 00:04:41.020
Me too, Gramps!

00:04:41.020 --> 00:04:41.890
Click!

00:04:43.760 --> 00:04:47.270
Do you really have to do this every morning?

00:04:47.660 --> 00:04:50.030
Let's dig in!

00:04:54.160 --> 00:04:57.320
By the way, when was Aoi coming back?

00:04:57.320 --> 00:04:58.240
Today!

00:05:04.160 --> 00:05:06.630
I'm going to pick her up right after school.

00:05:07.070 --> 00:05:08.380
Are you coming too, Momo?

00:05:08.380 --> 00:05:12.880
Sorry! The Pekoya is having a flash sale today.

00:05:12.880 --> 00:05:15.350
They're selling a carton of eggs for only ten yen!

00:05:15.350 --> 00:05:16.680
I can't let this chance slip away!

00:05:18.050 --> 00:05:19.900
So you aren't coming?

00:05:19.900 --> 00:05:22.850
Held back because of eggs? How petty.

00:05:23.360 --> 00:05:26.560
Whose fault is it again that we're poor?

00:05:28.770 --> 00:05:30.590
Uh... well, you see,

00:05:30.590 --> 00:05:33.950
those are absolutely essential to my research.

00:05:33.950 --> 00:05:37.720
What's a color spectrum analyzer?

00:05:37.720 --> 00:05:39.110
What do you use it for?

00:05:44.030 --> 00:05:46.860
So as I said, you'll have to go by yourself.

00:05:50.880 --> 00:05:52.660
Here, for the train.

00:05:54.530 --> 00:05:57.010
Is that gonna be enough to visit Mom?

00:05:57.010 --> 00:05:58.640
Don't worry.

00:05:58.640 --> 00:06:01.350
But if you don't hurry and eat, you're gonna be late.

00:06:02.400 --> 00:06:04.850
Whoa, it's already this late?!

00:06:06.050 --> 00:06:07.860
We're off!

00:06:07.860 --> 00:06:09.180
Take care!

00:06:11.190 --> 00:06:12.750
Now then...

00:06:22.010 --> 00:06:23.370
Whoops.

00:06:39.360 --> 00:06:41.520
I have to complete it quickly.

00:06:51.840 --> 00:06:55.410
Human 01 to Command. Current altitude 25000 feet.

00:06:56.370 --> 00:06:58.910
This is Command. Begin maneuvers.

00:06:59.650 --> 00:07:03.540
Rise to 35000 feet at azimuth 030.

00:07:03.920 --> 00:07:04.820
Roger.

00:07:08.730 --> 00:07:10.670
The US Army confirmed the target too.

00:07:10.670 --> 00:07:13.050
The surrounding countries claim it's not theirs.

00:07:13.430 --> 00:07:14.590
Reaching target!

00:07:26.110 --> 00:07:27.770
All units lost!

00:07:27.770 --> 00:07:30.150
Unidentified object disappeared from radar!

00:07:30.510 --> 00:07:32.630
What was that?!

00:07:33.350 --> 00:07:35.160
Issue emergency alert!

00:07:35.160 --> 00:07:37.910
Call the chiefs! Top priority!

00:07:40.660 --> 00:07:45.070
Next time in gym, junior and senior high are playing dodgeball together!

00:07:45.070 --> 00:07:46.880
Woohoo!

00:07:46.880 --> 00:07:48.170
Yay!

00:07:48.170 --> 00:07:50.100
We'll win for sure this time!

00:07:50.920 --> 00:07:53.260
Oh right, Isshiki!

00:07:53.260 --> 00:07:54.180
Yes?

00:07:54.710 --> 00:07:56.800
Really? Aoi is?

00:07:56.800 --> 00:08:00.570
Yeah. She did miss a lot classes,

00:08:00.570 --> 00:08:02.810
but she <i>is</i> sick, and she managed to finish her assignments properly,

00:08:02.810 --> 00:08:07.340
so we decided to let her move up to the next grade with you.

00:08:08.480 --> 00:08:10.570
Woohoo!

00:08:12.570 --> 00:08:14.570
I can't wait to tell Momo!

00:08:15.570 --> 00:08:16.570
Akane!

00:08:17.600 --> 00:08:19.200
What's wrong?

00:08:19.200 --> 00:08:20.830
Yu's in trouble!

00:08:27.640 --> 00:08:29.230
Stop it!

00:08:29.230 --> 00:08:29.920
Just a little more...

00:08:29.920 --> 00:08:30.710
Hey, just stop!

00:08:30.710 --> 00:08:32.050
What are you doing?!

00:08:38.920 --> 00:08:40.290
Aka...

00:08:41.610 --> 00:08:44.880
That was close. Why would you climb up there?

00:08:44.880 --> 00:08:48.900
This cute little guy fell out of his nest and got caught on a branch.

00:08:51.540 --> 00:08:53.570
Poor little birdy.

00:08:54.220 --> 00:08:56.780
Don't worry! Leave it to me!

00:09:08.870 --> 00:09:10.170
Aka...

00:09:15.050 --> 00:09:16.600
Akane?

00:09:16.600 --> 00:09:18.600
Are you okay, Aka?

00:09:22.780 --> 00:09:24.460
What are you doing, Isshiki?!

00:09:24.460 --> 00:09:25.580
Get down already!

00:09:30.840 --> 00:09:33.360
I'm so glad...

00:09:35.920 --> 00:09:40.620
You know you're no good with heights, so why?

00:09:41.720 --> 00:09:45.630
I really like how you try so hard, but it worries me too.

00:09:47.330 --> 00:09:49.340
Sorry, Momo.

00:09:59.300 --> 00:10:00.890
Sorry for the wait!

00:10:02.070 --> 00:10:08.120
Thank you very much for sending a plane just for me.

00:10:08.120 --> 00:10:11.280
Though I would love to return to the island as soon as possible.

00:10:11.680 --> 00:10:13.780
Just leave it to us, milady.

00:10:13.780 --> 00:10:21.040
This is the newest tiltrotor that uses Blue Island's Energy Rain System.

00:10:21.730 --> 00:10:24.540
We can promise you a phenomenal flight.

00:10:32.820 --> 00:10:34.430
Akane...

00:10:35.160 --> 00:10:38.180
I'll see you soon! Just a little longer.

00:10:43.300 --> 00:10:46.610
Aoi says she's headed here on a plane.

00:10:46.610 --> 00:10:48.820
Then we need to hurry!

00:10:49.320 --> 00:10:50.690
Yeah!

00:10:51.140 --> 00:10:52.800
See you guys later!

00:10:52.800 --> 00:10:55.080
See ya!

00:11:17.210 --> 00:11:19.010
Wh-What is that?!

00:11:30.360 --> 00:11:34.610
Then you are certain that this place is the enemy's target,

00:11:35.080 --> 00:11:36.070
Mr. President?

00:11:36.070 --> 00:11:37.790
Yes. It's either a terrorist attack,

00:11:37.790 --> 00:11:43.590
or some country is eyeing the Manifestor Engine.

00:11:43.590 --> 00:11:46.130
Must you insist humans are responsible?

00:11:46.610 --> 00:11:49.830
What else do you suggest there might be, Governor?

00:11:49.830 --> 00:11:55.190
Or do you mean to imply it's that "Alone" he was talking about?

00:11:56.000 --> 00:11:57.700
Initiating countermeasures.

00:11:57.700 --> 00:12:01.330
Please notify me if there are any changes.

00:12:02.740 --> 00:12:06.280
<i>Seven years ago no one listened to you</i>

00:12:06.280 --> 00:12:10.600
<i>and you were outcast for your alleged responsibility in the accident,</i>

00:12:11.320 --> 00:12:13.780
but now I think you might have been right,<i></i>

00:12:14.460 --> 00:12:16.280
Dr. Isshiki.<i></i>

00:12:17.780 --> 00:12:20.790
Damn Alones... So they're here after all.

00:12:21.910 --> 00:12:24.790
But this time it won't go your way.

00:12:29.870 --> 00:12:30.420
What was that?

00:12:33.440 --> 00:12:35.140
It's our place!

00:12:35.140 --> 00:12:44.560
Gramps!

00:12:47.320 --> 00:12:48.820
Are you okay, Gramps?!

00:12:49.100 --> 00:12:50.630
Gramps!

00:12:54.480 --> 00:12:56.570
He's not breathing.

00:12:57.190 --> 00:12:58.330
No way...

00:12:59.100 --> 00:13:00.080
Oh no...

00:13:00.830 --> 00:13:04.240
Gramps! Gramps!

00:13:04.240 --> 00:13:05.960
Gramps!

00:13:06.660 --> 00:13:08.030
What?

00:13:08.790 --> 00:13:11.470
Oh crap, I thought I was gonna die.

00:13:14.200 --> 00:13:15.340
Heave-ho.

00:13:16.230 --> 00:13:18.350
It's the stuffed animal I gave him!

00:13:18.620 --> 00:13:20.020
It's talking!

00:13:25.770 --> 00:13:29.030
What the hell?!

00:13:31.920 --> 00:13:34.450
It seems I managed to confine the manifestation,

00:13:34.450 --> 00:13:38.030
but I couldn't cancel out the shockwave from the transfer.

00:13:38.030 --> 00:13:42.910
My mind was ejected from my body.

00:13:42.910 --> 00:13:45.720
So you aren't dead or anything?

00:13:45.720 --> 00:13:46.780
Of course not!

00:13:46.780 --> 00:13:48.740
But that doesn't matter at all!

00:13:48.740 --> 00:13:50.550
Yes it does!

00:13:50.550 --> 00:13:52.430
Do not fret, my grandchildren!

00:13:52.430 --> 00:13:55.050
I'll eventually find a way to return to my body.

00:13:55.050 --> 00:13:57.100
But more importantly...

00:13:57.670 --> 00:13:59.470
I finally completed it!

00:13:59.470 --> 00:14:00.920
Completed what?

00:14:00.920 --> 00:14:02.130
What is it?

00:14:02.130 --> 00:14:04.000
Look at my hand!

00:14:05.900 --> 00:14:08.100
Not here, there!

00:14:11.780 --> 00:14:12.900
What's this?

00:14:12.900 --> 00:14:16.550
I spent half my life on my research, and at last, it's borne fruit.

00:14:16.550 --> 00:14:20.830
In a way, the Manifestor Engine was just a byproduct in creating this.

00:14:21.260 --> 00:14:23.280
A key?

00:14:23.280 --> 00:14:26.330
Akane! Only you can use that key.

00:14:26.330 --> 00:14:28.010
Take it!

00:14:28.010 --> 00:14:29.840
Only me?

00:14:34.120 --> 00:14:35.140
What?

00:14:35.720 --> 00:14:41.140
This is an announcement from Tokyo for New Oshima.

00:14:42.470 --> 00:14:47.540
New Oshima and the rest of the Izu archipelago are now in a state of emergency.

00:14:47.540 --> 00:14:49.050
I wonder what happened.

00:14:49.050 --> 00:14:50.650
Is it Mt. Mihara?

00:14:50.650 --> 00:14:53.640
No. Even an eruption would be preferable.

00:14:53.640 --> 00:14:56.410
The greatest possible disaster is approaching Blue Island!

00:14:56.770 --> 00:14:58.650
Blue Island?

00:14:59.240 --> 00:15:00.120
Aoi!

00:15:08.120 --> 00:15:11.380
For now, let's just keep my body there.

00:15:11.840 --> 00:15:13.680
Th-The fridge?

00:15:15.640 --> 00:15:18.150
Momo, you go underground!

00:15:18.150 --> 00:15:20.600
Not even a bunker buster could scratch that place.

00:15:21.750 --> 00:15:24.190
Watch the house, Momo!

00:15:24.190 --> 00:15:29.360
We promised we'd protect it until Mom's out of the hospital, after all!

00:15:29.360 --> 00:15:30.470
Yeah.

00:15:31.120 --> 00:15:32.750
Let's go, Gramps!

00:15:34.680 --> 00:15:38.890
Blue Island personnel evacuated. Use of missiles permitted.

00:15:38.890 --> 00:15:39.620
Roger!

00:15:39.620 --> 00:15:43.430
All units, fire at will! We will soon acquire visual!

00:15:48.360 --> 00:15:50.100
Th-That's the enemy?

00:15:50.100 --> 00:15:51.460
Watch out! Split up!

00:15:53.430 --> 00:15:54.670
Beam weapons?

00:15:59.430 --> 00:16:01.490
We don't wanna get hit by the waves!

00:16:01.490 --> 00:16:03.230
Get as high as possible!

00:16:03.230 --> 00:16:03.940
Got it!

00:16:09.350 --> 00:16:11.400
What's flashing over there?

00:16:11.400 --> 00:16:14.520
The army's engaging the Alone.

00:16:14.520 --> 00:16:15.990
What a futile effort.

00:16:15.990 --> 00:16:16.820
"Alone"?

00:16:22.220 --> 00:16:24.340
Status code 104.

00:16:24.340 --> 00:16:27.670
The nuclear induction device has suffered serious structural damage.

00:16:27.670 --> 00:16:29.670
The chain reaction is out of control.

00:16:30.240 --> 00:16:33.960
Mom, we're so high up! I'm scared!

00:16:33.960 --> 00:16:36.400
You mustn't look down, Akane!

00:16:36.400 --> 00:16:39.750
We'll be fine. They're coming to help us.

00:16:44.660 --> 00:16:47.750
Mashiro! I'm coming right away! Hold on!

00:16:52.110 --> 00:16:53.400
What on Earth is that?!

00:17:01.950 --> 00:17:05.360
Mashiro! Akane!

00:17:06.960 --> 00:17:09.300
Its target is the Manifestor Engine!

00:17:09.510 --> 00:17:11.330
The Engine? Why?

00:17:11.330 --> 00:17:15.470
I don't know! But if the Engine gets destroyed, it'll be the end of the world!

00:17:15.470 --> 00:17:17.180
Hurry, Akane!

00:17:36.200 --> 00:17:37.410
It sunk the Adamant!

00:17:37.880 --> 00:17:39.350
Damn. How dare they!

00:17:39.350 --> 00:17:41.260
Concentrate, lieutenant!

00:17:41.260 --> 00:17:42.400
But...

00:17:44.610 --> 00:17:47.960
A civilian plane? What's it doing here?!

00:18:02.600 --> 00:18:05.440
Civilian aircraft! Vacate this airspace immediately!

00:18:05.440 --> 00:18:07.980
There's no way! I can't control the plane!

00:18:11.000 --> 00:18:12.180
Horrible...

00:18:18.530 --> 00:18:21.880
Aoi! Aoi's on that!

00:18:21.880 --> 00:18:23.160
This is bad, Akane!

00:18:23.160 --> 00:18:25.670
It's gonna crash straight into the Engine!

00:18:31.180 --> 00:18:32.800
Akane...

00:18:35.040 --> 00:18:38.190
If you go straight ahead, there'll be a lift to the top!

00:18:38.190 --> 00:18:39.260
Straight ahead!

00:18:56.870 --> 00:18:58.770
Prepare for emergency landing!

00:18:58.770 --> 00:18:59.620
Roger!

00:18:59.620 --> 00:19:02.870
Milady, prepare for impact!

00:19:09.440 --> 00:19:11.900
Hurry! Hurry!

00:19:18.010 --> 00:19:19.010
Aoi!

00:19:24.800 --> 00:19:27.020
Oh my...

00:19:29.660 --> 00:19:31.240
Aoi!

00:19:34.220 --> 00:19:35.530
Akane...

00:19:35.790 --> 00:19:37.530
Aoi!

00:19:40.600 --> 00:19:43.580
We're so high up! I'm scared!

00:19:45.040 --> 00:19:47.710
No!

00:19:59.040 --> 00:20:00.720
Akane...

00:20:01.940 --> 00:20:03.190
Aoi...

00:20:04.780 --> 00:20:06.340
Akane...

00:20:06.340 --> 00:20:07.440
Don't come...

00:20:09.460 --> 00:20:10.940
Aoi...

00:20:23.870 --> 00:20:25.370
Akane!

00:20:34.630 --> 00:20:37.600
Go!

00:20:42.390 --> 00:20:44.850
Aoi!

00:20:45.850 --> 00:20:47.110
Akane!

00:21:39.400 --> 00:21:42.080
Akane, we're flying!

00:21:42.080 --> 00:21:43.920
Oh, really?

00:21:44.320 --> 00:21:47.040
Akane, we're up really high!

00:21:47.470 --> 00:21:50.050
Don't worry, I'm not scared anymore!

00:21:50.540 --> 00:21:52.550
Operation successful!

00:21:52.550 --> 00:21:57.210
This is the power of my greatest invention, the Vivid System!

00:21:57.210 --> 00:21:58.810
Vivid System?

00:22:05.040 --> 00:22:06.180
That's...

00:22:06.740 --> 00:22:09.020
The enemy broke through the second line of defense.

00:22:09.020 --> 00:22:10.650
It'll make landfall at this rate.

00:22:18.770 --> 00:22:19.910
The city!

00:22:20.210 --> 00:22:21.680
Do you want to help?

00:22:22.820 --> 00:22:28.990
In this world, you and <i>only</i> you have the power to fight the Alones!

00:22:31.880 --> 00:22:32.760
Sure!

00:22:32.760 --> 00:22:33.930
Yes!

00:22:34.330 --> 00:22:36.430
Very well. Listen closely!

00:22:37.120 --> 00:22:38.430
It's docking time!

00:22:39.430 --> 00:22:40.810
Docking?

00:24:14.280 --> 00:24:16.720
Greetings! I am Futaba Aoi.

00:24:16.720 --> 00:24:19.580
Our new and suddenly appearing enemy, the Alone,

00:24:19.580 --> 00:24:22.410
is truly frightening, but I can fight as long as I'm by Akane's side!

00:24:22.410 --> 00:24:24.700
Next time - When They Overlap.

00:24:24.710 --> 00:24:26.950
We'll protect everyone for sure!
